From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: perlytiara <12584332+perlytiara@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:12:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Vault fork: say "No server yet" instead of a generic
 error

On the phone the owner typed an email and a master password and got
Bitwarden's "An error has occurred": the built-in server address is still a
placeholder (a host under .invalid), so the request could not go anywhere.

- Login screen: a note under the server selector while the server is a
  placeholder; Continue and Create account open a "No server yet" message
  before anything else is typed. Same guard on the create-account screen.
- Login: when the server does not answer at all (unknown name, refused,
  timeout) the dialog names the server and suggests what to check, instead of
  "We were unable to process your request".
- Environment.isPlaceholderServer in the data module; our own texts in
  app/src/main/res/values/vault_strings.xml (they never name the app).
- Tests for the three view models and the placeholder check; the upstream
  default-server test follows the fork's default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
